---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="How It Works · The Cheapskate Club"
  description="App-synced, honestly labeled, and strictly frugal."
>
  <section class="prose" style="max-width: 760px; margin: 40px auto; padding: 0 20px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">BE CHEAP. DON’T BE A CHEAT.</p>
    <h1>
      A scoreboard.<br />
      <em>Not an audit.</em>
    </h1>

    <h2>App-synced, honestly labeled</h2>
    <p>
      Rankings use reported, settled usage from opted-in cheapoS installations.
      Installation signatures help detect changed submissions and duplicate uploads.
      They do not prove that a modified app is reporting genuine inference.
    </p>

    <h2>Every token counts</h2>
    <p>
      One score adds free remote, included-access, and local-model tokens. Tokens reflect
      real machine telemetry across public free tiers, included account quotas, local
      hardware, and precision paid spend. Unverified estimates and imported history stay
      out of rankings. Monthly rankings use UTC.
    </p>

    <h2>Private by default</h2>
    <p>
      No prompts, source code, project paths, or provider credentials belong in a
      leaderboard upload. Model names are optional: choose whether to send them from
      cheapoS and display them on your profile.
    </p>

    <h2>Why cheapoS.lol?</h2>
    <p>
      Because spending $70/year on a <code>.ai</code> domain would violate our core terms
      of service. We build on small bills, lean compute, and honest code. Proudly operated
      on a $1.80/year domain.
    </p>

    <h2>Still taking shape</h2>
    <p>
      Installation pairing and signed usage sync are active. If you want to benchmark
      your agent runs or sponsor the club, check our prospectus.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top: 32px;">
      <a class="button primary" href="/leaderboard">
        View Leaderboard ↗
      </a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/sponsors" style="margin-left: 12px;">
        Sponsor prospectus ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
